      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a bit hard to read due to many conditions and reverse order of pushing. What do you think we change this to:\n```\nRenderPassColorAttachment msaaStorePassAttachment \u003d {};\nmsaaStorePassAttachment.view \u003d deferredResolve.copySrc.Get();\nmsaaStorePassAttachment.loadOp \u003d wgpu::LoadOp::Load;\nmsaaStorePassAttachment.storeOp \u003d deferredResolve.storeOp;\n\nif (partialResolve) {\n   auto resolvePassCallback \u003d ResolveMultisampleWithDraw(...);\n   \n   passEndOperations.emplace_back([\u003d]{\n      // Do partial resolve first in one render pass.\n      resolvePassCallback();\n      // Then fulfill the original store op for MSAA texture in another render\n      // pass.\n      // Note: no need to fulfill if the storeOp \u003d Store because we already do\n      // that in the main render pass.\n      if (deferredResolve.storeOp !\u003d wgpu::StoreOp::Store) {\n         // Start render pass with msaaStorePassAttachment\n         BeginRenderPass(...);\n         End(...);\n      }\n   });\n}\nelse {\n   passEndOperations.emplace_back([\u003d]{\n     // Resolve the MSAA texture into the resolve texture in a dedicated pass.\n     msaaStorePassAttachment.resolveTarget \u003d deferredResolve.copyDst.Get();\n     BeginRenderPass(...);\n     End(...);\n   });\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, I think it\u0027s not necessary to fulfill the Discard storeOp by adding another render pass. We could simple call `texture-\u003eSetInitialized(false)`. WDYT Corentin \u0026 Austin?",
